</code>
In this case, we are checking if the return value (`RET`) is greater than or equal to the old count of the list (`OLD(COUNT)`). This will ensure that we do not remove an element that does not exist in the list. The `RET` and `OLD(COUNT)` are referring to the return value from the `Add` method (the new size of the list after appending a new value) and the old count of the list respectively.
